  "result": "Perfect! All 72 tests pass \u2713\n\n**Summary of additions:**\n\n1. **src/invoices.js** \u2014 Two new edit functions:\n   - `addLine(invoice, { sku, qty })` \u2014 Adds a new line to a draft invoice, or if the SKU already exists, increases that line's qty. Validates qty and SKU existence like createInvoice. Returns `fail('NOT_DRAFT')` if the invoice status isn't 'draft'.\n   - `removeLine(invoice, sku)` \u2014 Removes the line with the given SKU from a draft invoice. Returns `fail('NOT_DRAFT')` if not draft, `fail('LINE_NOT_FOUND')` if SKU isn't on the invoice, and `fail('NO_LINES')` if it would remove the last line.\n\n2. **src/errors.js** \u2014 Two new error codes:\n   - `NOT_DRAFT`: \"Only draft invoices can be edited.\"\n   - `LINE_NOT_FOUND`: \"That SKU is not on this invoice.\"\n\n3. **test/invoices.test.js** \u2014 20 new tests covering:\n   - Adding new lines to single-line and multi-line invoices\n   - Increasing qty on existing SKUs\n   - All validation errors (invalid qty, unknown SKU)\n   - Status checks (NOT_DRAFT)\n   - Removing lines and edge cases (last line, not found)\n   - Non-mutation of original invoices\n   - Complex workflows (add then remove, multiple adds of same SKU)\n\nBoth functions respect the house rules: they don't mutate arguments, return result types, and validate input.",
